hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-11 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-11 = cons "*Language* is from *lingua*, tongue. *Tongue* is how humans transmitted knowledge before scratching it, and the word is still the body part. A language of languages is a tongue of tongues. *Interface* is *inter* + *facies*, between faces. Human–computer interaction is, in the old word, the place between faces. A face is what's turned toward you; *versus*, again, toward." (cons "" nil)
